WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.335
-Thank you so much.
Nice to see you.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.703
Thank you for tuning in
and watching

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.205
"The Tonight Show," everybody.
Nice to see you, Roots.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:08.308
I had a dream about you
last night, Quest.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.343
-Me?
-Yeah.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:14.713
I had a -- I had Indian food,
which I love.

00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:16.215
-[ Laughs ]
-It's my favorite.

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:17.684
-He's laughing already.
-What?

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.152
I had -- you know
I like the spicy, man.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:21.988
-This can't end well.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.690
-No, it ends -- It's not bad.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.926
It was just an odd dream.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.796
So, I had --
Chicken vindaloo is my jam.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:32.298
So I go super spicy.
I'm not afraid.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.500
And then I don't know
if my brain can handle it,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.171
so I went to sleep, my slumber,

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.939
and I was in --
everything was great.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.107
And then I started
having these dreams.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.708
We were doing the show.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.276
And in the middle of the show,

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:45.879
it was back
when we had the crowd,

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.647
and in the middle of the show,
you stopped me, and you go,

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.083
"Jimmy, stop. I got to just show
you something, man."

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.284
I go, "What's up?"

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.554
And you walked around
behind James over there,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.055
and you just started dancing.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:59.125
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.962
Like, almost like a ballerina
type of a --

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.932
like, you were spinning around,
and, like, doing that thing

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.366
where you keep
kicking and spinning.

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:08.968
-Isn't that called a pirouette?

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.069
-What?
-A pirouette.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.271
-Yeah, yeah,
it was like a pirouette,

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.905
but it was one of
those impressive ones

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:16.475
where it doesn't end, really,
and just keeps going.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.044
-Like "White Knights" the movie,
okay.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.912
-Yes, it was Baryshnikov.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.548
-Rubles, rubles, rubles.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:23.950
Wait, why do I remember
that reference?

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.651
-Dude, rubles, rubles, rubles.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:28.054
So, it was that happening,
and I go --

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.256
And at one point I was
a little kind of embarrassed

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.590
because I go like,
"What is he doing?"

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.459
And then I go, "That's pretty
impressive, actually."

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.094
I loved it.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.930
And then these people
were in the front row

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.264
and they all had matching
T-shirts and they go,

00:01:39.264 --> 00:01:40.867
"We're dancers, too."

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:41.935
And they got up
and started doing --

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.236
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.971
I woke up like 5:00
in the morning.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.839
I was going to text you like,

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:49.342
"I don't know what's going on,
man." But anyways.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:52.812
-When I get down to
my goal weight of 200 pounds,

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.346
I'm going to do that.
-Alright, good.

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:56.916
That's probably what it is.
[ Applause ]

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.651
That's what it is.
-Alright.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.453
-Alright. Let's get
to the news and jokes.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:03.689
Well, guys, President Trump
is still down in the polls,

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.591
so he's trying everything
to help his campaign.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:07.760
And I got to admit,
I did not see this one coming.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.061
Listen to this one.

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.596
-In a tweet this morning,
he wrote,

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:11.897
"With universal mail-in voting,

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:13.466
not absentee voting,
which is good,

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.135
2020 will be
the most inaccurate

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.136
and fraudulent election
in history.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.171
It will be a great embarrassment
to the USA.

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:21.240
Delay the election
until people can properly,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.743
securely and safely vote."

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:28.681
-He wants to delay the election.
It's the presidential election.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.883
It's not the release date
for "Bill and Ted 3."

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.052
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.888
When they saw Trump's tweet,
JetBlue is like, "Trust us.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.390
When he says delayed,
he means canceled."

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.059
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.761
"We've done it enough times."

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.928
Americans were like,

00:02:42.928 --> 00:02:44.897
"How long a delay
are we talking about here?

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.732
Months, like your response
to COVID?

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.334
Years, like your response
to Putin?

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.203
Or decades,
like a hug for Don Jr.?

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:54.173
Just give us a hint."

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.842
If he can't deny it,
pretty soon he'll be like

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:59.344
"Republicans
should all vote on November 3rd,

00:02:59.344 --> 00:03:03.249
but we'll have Democrats vote
at a later date, TBD."

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.717
I don't think Trump
wants to leave.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.018
He's like that friend who's been

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:07.353
crashing at your house
for a while

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:11.057
but keeps dropping hints
he might need some more time.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.159
You see how Trump used
three question marks

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.061
at the end of his tweet.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.564
Yeah, I don't think the
President should ever be using

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.466
three question marks,
I mean, I don't even want

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.433
my mechanic doing that.

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:23.369
It's like,
"Need new brakes maybe?"

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.071
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.472
Stop with the question marks.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.075
The last thing our country needs
right now is a cliffhanger.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.943
And it's not just Democrats.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.578
Many Republicans
like Lindsey Graham,

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.180
Mitch McConnell and Ted Cruz

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.148
have also come out
against the idea.

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:38.050
Yeah, not since Trump's
last 10 ideas

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.787
has everyone agreed
that this is a really bad idea.

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.956
Even during the worst times
in U.S. history,

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.492
the presidential election
has never been postponed,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.995
not for the Civil War,
not for the pandemic of 1918,

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:52.865
and not even for the Ed Hardy
T-shirt fad of 2008.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.336
-Hey.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.338
-Were you one of those guys?

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:00.206
-No, Jimmy. Shut up, Tariq!

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:04.443
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:05.678
-I know.
-They were free.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.746
-No, I know they were.
I know they were.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.516
Yeah, they were free.
Oh, my God.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.986
Lately it hasn't been easy
for Trump's campaign.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:16.421
Let's see if they were able
to turn things around today.

00:04:16.421 --> 00:04:18.791
-Journalists in Vice President
Mike Pence's motorcade

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.561
say his bus
was involved in a minor crash

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:24.329
with a dump truck
on the way to Greensburg.

00:04:24.329 --> 00:04:26.232
-Don't worry, everyone is okay.

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.634
Actually, a campaign bus
hitting a garbage truck

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.304
pretty much sums up
Trump's last six months.

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.739
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:37.943
Well, luckily, the accident only
caused a minor fender bender

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:39.678
and a small oil leak.

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:42.014
And I'm talking about Pence,
not the bus.

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:44.517
Oil can, oil can, oil can.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.651
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.120
A little Wizard of Oz ref.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.756
Well, guys, yesterday during
an interview with ABC News,

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:53.626
Dr. Fauci mentioned
a new safety measure to defend

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.561
against the coronavirus.
Watch this.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.798
-Dr. Anthony Fauci now touting
another possible tool

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.367
to fight the virus --
eye protection.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.737
-If you have goggles
or an eye shield,

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:05.905
you should use it.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.874
I mean, it's not
universally recommended,

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:10.576
but if you really want
to be complete,

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.645
you should probably use it.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.580
-Yeah, the President wouldn't
even wear glasses

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.016
during an eclipse.
There's no way he's doing this.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:20.519
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.555
People are like, "I don't know,
I don't want to look stupid."

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.890
And then they went back
to wearing a mask

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.191
with Skeletor's teeth on it.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.192
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.192 --> 00:05:29.195
I feel like we're one week away
from Dr. Fauci

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:31.030
telling everyone to walk
around in a beekeeper suit.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.531
Am I right?

00:05:32.531 --> 00:05:34.700
Hopefully the goggles
will protect you from the virus

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.337
and if Dr. Fauci was anywhere
near you with a baseball.

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:45.177
Hey, you know, he was thinking
like, "Good, good, good.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:46.312
Oh, it's bad,
it's bad, it's bad."

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.581
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:51.784
Hey, guys, here's some exciting
news for sports fans.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:55.054
-Basketball bouncing back with
a doubleheader in the bubble.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.822
For more than three weeks,

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:59.092
players from 22 teams
have been training

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.359
and living at Disney World.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:03.262
344 players
have repeatedly been tested

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.197
for coronavirus in the bubble,

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:07.533
and not a single test
has come back positive.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.768
-Yeah!
The NBA is back.

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:11.337
Only the top 22 teams

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:13.539
were invited to
the Disney World bubble.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.308
The other eight are just
playing scrimmages

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:16.809
in a parking lot
behind Chuck E. Cheese.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:18.644
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.213
Well, this is weird. Even though
the NBA is back tonight,

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:23.782
ESPN still showed three hours
of arm wrestling.

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:25.451
Isn't that weird?

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:30.289
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:34.026
"I don't know if he's going to
go over the top with this one.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.729
He's gonna go over the top.
He's got him!"

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.703
It's been
a crazy week in sports.

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.438
That's what I'd say.

00:06:46.438 --> 00:06:48.807
Between the NBA starting today,

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:51.310
Major League Baseball
and the NFL

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.345
is thinking about their season,
which means it's time for

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.447
"Oof, Yeesh, Oh, God."

00:06:55.447 --> 00:06:58.985
♪ -Oof, yeesh, oh, God ♪

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.519
-That's right. The NFL is hoping

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:01.887
they can still have
a season this year,

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.455
but things are already off
to a rocky start.

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:04.857
Take a look at this.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:08.227
-A new reality for the NFL
with more than a dozen players

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.796
already opting out
of the 2020 season

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:12.298
by the first day
of training camp.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:15.234
-Ooh. Players are already
dropping out.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.202
♪ -Oof ♪

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:18.904
-Of course, Major League
Baseball has already

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:21.440
started their season. Let's see
how that's going so far.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:25.144
-ESPN reporting that the Miami
Marlins home opener tonight

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:27.113
has been canceled.
Eight more players

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:31.183
and two coaches have now
tested positive for coronavirus.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:33.018
-Seriously?
That's now 14 players.

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:35.120
♪ -Yeesh ♪

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.223
-Well, at least I'm sure the NBA
isn't having any issues

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:39.058
after putting players
in their bubbles.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:41.794
-The NBA is investigating
what Clippers guard Lou Williams

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:45.297
did on his recent excused
absence from the NBA bubble.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:48.000
ESPN reports that Williams
told NBA security

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.368
that he went
to a funeral in Atlanta

00:07:50.368 --> 00:07:53.973
and after that, he went
to a strip club for dinner.

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:56.042
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:59.378
-Dude, a strip club to eat?

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:00.713
♪ -Oh, God ♪

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:02.248
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:05.584
And this has been
"Oof, Yeesh, Oh, God."

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:08.988
♪ -Oof, yeesh, oh, God ♪

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:11.090
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.659
-This is exciting, guys.

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:14.827
Today after --

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.128
I don't know who was
hitting the high note.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.429
I don't know who was
hitting the high notes, but --

00:08:17.429 --> 00:08:19.531
-Acknowledge that greatness.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.531 --> 00:08:20.866
Go ahead, man.
Take some time now.

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:22.034
Acknowledge the greatness.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:24.003
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.371
-[ High-pitched voice ]
♪ Oh, God ♪

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:27.973
[ Laughter ]

00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:29.809
[ Normal voice ] Well, guys,
some business news

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:31.176
that we could probably do
without.

00:08:31.176 --> 00:08:35.413
French's is releasing
a limited time mustard beer

00:08:35.413 --> 00:08:37.950
in celebration of National
Mustard Day this Saturday.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.585
Let's take a look at this.

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:42.922
Yeah, finally, we no longer
have to squirt some French's

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:46.058
into our Bud Light.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.058 --> 00:08:48.193
If you want to buy it,
good news --

00:08:48.193 --> 00:08:49.695
all the cases
are still available.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:53.566
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:54.933
Some people are
a little classier --

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:57.536
prefer a Grey Poupon Zinfandel.

00:08:57.536 --> 00:09:00.139
Meanwhile, you know, we've all
got that friend who's like,

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.675
"I only drink
artisanal mustard beer.

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:05.077
So do you have
any Sir Kensington's?"

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:06.945
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.945 --> 00:09:10.049
"I guess I won't drink."

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.149
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.149 --> 00:09:15.020
"Just don't feel like it.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.656
Not in the mood."

00:09:17.656 --> 00:09:23.128
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.128 --> 00:09:25.631
And finally these days can feel

00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:27.166
like there's a lot
going wrong in the world.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:29.134
Sometimes you just wish
you could make it right.

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:31.370
Well, luckily, we're able to do
that here at "The Tonight Show."

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.006
We took this week's
biggest stories and changed them

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:35.374
to what we wish had happened.

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:36.942
It's time for
"This Week Made Right."

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:38.077
Check it out.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:43.649 line:0%
♪♪

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:46.919
-Dr. Anthony Fauci
to throw out the first pitch.

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:48.554
Yeah.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:55.160
-We want a vaccine available
for the American people.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:10:01.100
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.434
-Alright, welcome back.

00:10:02.434 --> 00:10:04.603
Republicans now say they want
to send many Americans

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:07.906
another round of $1.2 million
stimulus checks.

00:10:07.906 --> 00:10:10.576
Today, White House officials
and Senate Republicans announced

00:10:10.576 --> 00:10:12.011
they are working out
the details.

00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:13.379
-As the weather gets warmer,

00:10:13.379 --> 00:10:15.747
there has been an uptick
in maskless people

00:10:15.747 --> 00:10:17.182
going to crowded parties.

00:10:17.182 --> 00:10:20.219
But don't worry. They have
all been put in NASA's rocket

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:23.755
and launched straight to Mars.

00:10:23.755 --> 00:10:25.758
-We have a great show
for you tonight.

